                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a0f8811b-0f3b-367e-9188-da63c70dfaa1",
                                        "entry_id": "031438b5-c1ed-357a-ad96-f66e03d4cfd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to Juan Perón or his regime."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c0ba952-ee08-4e02-a0d6-262d62afeeb9",
                                                "sense_id": "a0f8811b-0f3b-367e-9188-da63c70dfaa1",
                                                "text": "In a last frantic move, the Peronist government again turned to a stringent stabilization plan (i.e. another 100 per cent peso devaluation, 90 per cent increases in publicly-controlled prices, coupled with a meagre 20 per cent increase in nominal wages). [...] Some idea of this incredibly rapid 'Weimarization' of Argentine politics can be gleaned from an extrapolation of the first quarter's inflation to a 3,000 per cent annual rate. Using the March figure, the same calculation yields a fantastic 17,000 per cent annual rate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb150c5d-62ab-302b-961e-8bd22fa1dfe2",
                                        "entry_id": "031438b5-c1ed-357a-ad96-f66e03d4cfd4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Adhering to or describing modern-day Peronism, including any of the political parties that self-identify as such."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5509448-eaa2-408c-b87e-a1f65fb554fe",
                                                "sense_id": "cb150c5d-62ab-302b-961e-8bd22fa1dfe2",
                                                "text": "In suburban Buenos Aires, Milei’s Peronist rival, the finance minister, Sergio Massa, asked factory workers for support despite the slump his government has overseen, with 40% of Argentina’s 47 million citizens living in poverty amid triple-digit inflation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
